visualVerdict:
Total 30/40, the low end of Good. The engineering content is good: each view is focused and honest about its scope, every edge is labelled, failure behaviour is specific, and the facts I spot-checked against the source match. Visually, though, the user's \"messy\" is fair. It does not come from tangled lines. It comes from:
- tiny single-red type everywhere, with no visual hierarchy;
- a prose footer that eats a quarter to a third of every view;
- edges cutting through frame header text;
- step order that zig-zags in the fleet view;
- one view (the agent→Claude view) partly hidden under the app's tool palette.
At 1194×834 it can be read only with zooming. Raising type size, a safe-area margin and cleaner edge routing would fix most of what feels unusable without changing the content.
